  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Algebraic Laws of Complex Conjugation}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Theorem:\ngiven: z, w is \\complex\nthen:\n. \\complex.conjugate(z \\.complex.+./ w) = \\complex.conjugate(z) \\.complex.+./ \\complex.conjugate(w)\n. \\complex.conjugate(z \\.complex.*./ w) = \\complex.conjugate(z) \\.complex.*./ \\complex.conjugate(w)\n. z \\.complex.*./ \\complex.conjugate(z) = \\complex.modulus(z) \\.real.*./ \\complex.modulus(z)\n. if: z != \\complex.zero\n  then: \\complex.one \\.complex.div./ z = \\complex.conjugate(z) \\.complex.div./ (\\complex.modulus(z) \\.real.*./ \\complex.modulus(z))\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Algebraic Laws of Complex Conjugation\"\n. description: \"Conjugation preserves addition and multiplication, and its\n                product with the original number is the squared modulus.\"\nId: \"bdb7d794-5eb2-41f5-823f-5f4f719266a3\"",
